# Chrome extension dev — agent vs extension reload

## Agents (automatic — do not ask the user to restart the agent)

After changing `remotes/c_remote_browser/**` or before sheet batch writes when IPC/sheets ops fail:

1. Run from repo root: `.\_\scripts\dev\restart_chrome_remote_agent.ps1`
2. Call `browser.agent.restart` on the paired device (or rely on `browser.sheets.row_set` auto-retry).
3. Wait ~5s, then retry.

`browser.sheets.row_set` calls `agent.restart` and retries once on stale agent errors.

## Extension reload (automatic when possible)

After `sync_chrome_extension_install.ps1` or `restart_chrome_remote_agent.ps1` (syncs `install/alienai_remote`):

1. Call `browser.extension` with `op: ensure_updated` (or rely on `agent.ensure` on popup connect — SW reloads when install `manifest.json` version is newer).
2. Fallback: `browser.extension` `op: reload`.
3. Ask the user to use chrome://extensions **only** if install version matches but the SW is still stale (wrong unpacked load path).

Chrome must load the unpacked extension from `%LOCALAPPDATA%\AlienAI\chrome_extension\install\alienai_remote` for install-folder auto-update to apply.

## Sheet writes

Prefer `browser.sheets.row_set` for G-L, not six `cell_set` calls.